Aerie-Purpose: Make Blink skip legacy <link rel=prefetch> when the preloading pref (net.network_prediction_options) is Off, so the hardening promise "prefetch off" holds for link prefetch too.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc (OverrideWebPreferences), third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/preload_helper.cc (PrefetchIfNeeded)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Chromium gates speculation rules, prerender and preconnect on the pref in the browser
process, but the renderer fetches <link rel=prefetch> with no check, so the Bench
check hardening_prefetch saw a Sec-Purpose: prefetch request with the pref Off. The
browser already sends WebPreferences::dns_prefetching_enabled to Blink, and Chrome
never sets it (always true). This patch sets it from IsSomePreloadingEnabled and makes
PrefetchIfNeeded honour it. No new plumbing. Side effect: renderer DNS prefetch
(rel=dns-prefetch) is also off with the pref, as the pref's text says. The value is
read when a page's preferences are computed, so a change of the pref applies to
tabs from their next preference update (new tabs and navigations that recreate the view).

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -4728,6 +4728,12 @@
 
   web_prefs->default_encoding = prefs->GetString(prefs::kDefaultCharset);
 
+  // Aerie: Blink reads this to skip <link rel=prefetch> (and DNS prefetch)
+  // when the preloading pref is Off.
+  web_prefs->dns_prefetching_enabled =
+      prefetch::IsSomePreloadingEnabled(*prefs) ==
+      content::PreloadingEligibility::kEligible;
+
   web_prefs->dom_paste_enabled =
       prefs->GetBoolean(prefs::kWebKitDomPasteEnabled);
   web_prefs->javascript_can_access_clipboard =
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/preload_helper.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/preload_helper.cc
@@ -802,6 +802,10 @@
   if (!params.rel.IsLinkPrefetch() || !params.href.IsValid() ||
       !document.GetFrame())
     return;
+  // Aerie: no link prefetch when preloading is Off (the browser clears this).
+  if (document.GetSettings() &&
+      !document.GetSettings()->GetDNSPrefetchingEnabled())
+    return;
   UseCounter::Count(document, WebFeature::kLinkRelPrefetch);
 
   ResourceRequest resource_request(params.href);
